  "design_notes": [
    "All baseline rows carry the identical feature vector (10.0, 20.0): the HSTree mass concentrates on that single region, so an unseen point gets a much higher local score and the Welford mean+k*sigma verdict flips to anomaly reliably. Varied baselines spread the mass and make the verdict unreliable (measured locally).",
    "HSTREE_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE=100: events 1..99 return no local score, so v2 marks them warmup. Event 100 fills the initial window, initializes the model and gets a score.",
    "SHAP_BACKGROUND_SIZE is fixed to 100 in docker-compose, so the initial window must be >= 100: the background is already complete at initialization and no post-warmup event can be background_not_ready.",
    "HSTREE_ANOMALY_MIN_SAMPLES=2: the pipeline enforces max(2, ...) samples before a verdict. Events 100 and 101 are therefore post-warmup (score available, v2 status computed) with a still-null hstree_anomaly: they are declared explicitly as threshold_warmup_ids. From event 102 the verdict is strictly boolean.",
    "oc12-evt-104 (normal) and oc12-evt-105 (outlier) share timestamp 2026-09-18 12:01:43 and Group with distinct source_event_id values: the identity pair for Kafka and InfluxDB.",
    "Outliers repeat at events 105, 109 and 110 so the anomaly verdict has a comfortable margin."
  ],
  "threshold_warmup_ids": [
